      ],
      "deltaSummaryMarkdown": "Inspected the reworked `nesting.rs` (cost units per construct, the regex group cap, TypeScript postfix `!`, the fail-closed coarse bound with its short-source fast path) and the step-budget minimum in `engine.rs`, `mod.rs` and `token_resolution.rs`, plus the new tests named in each finding.\n\nI rebuilt the throwaway probe under `artifacts-temp/agentx/dtcg-expressions/probe` and probed with it:\n- every earlier crash case and new bypass attempts, in release on an 8 MiB thread;\n- a binary search of the deepest accepted source for 53 constructs, in debug on a 1 MiB thread;\n- the step-budget-0 sweep.\n\nNo input crashed or hung. I relied on the coordinator's passing check evidence and reran no test group.\n\nS1-F1 and S1-F9 are resolved; S1-F2..F8 stay resolved. No findings remain open.\n\nResidual note, not a finding: the accepted depths are calibrated for unoptimized code on a 1 MiB stack, so hosts resolving on much smaller threads keep less margin. The `stack_limit` doc already warns to leave room on the resolving thread's stack, and wasm32 is sprint 2's PLT-2.",
      "reattestedFrom": "37583003b07036fb228f6a9f18f37c053e85aaab79f11bc52209c88663ee4891",
      "summaryMarkdown": "EXP-1, PLT-1, EVAL-1..3 and EVAL-5 hold in source and tests (snapshot/type order, inputs through `resolve_value` at `Position::Unchecked` with cycle detection, integral/rounding/depth/node rules, dependency collection of inputs, export round trip); memory, stack and step trips are uncatchable as tested, Atomics cannot block, ReDoS stops at the step budget. The sprint fails on four major defects found by probes: oxc stack overflow aborts the host on deeply nested expression text (S1-F1), unfrozen shared intrinsics (tamed members, Promise, iterator helpers) let expressions affect each other (S1-F2), the step budget depends on prior evaluations through QuickJS's interrupt counter (S1-F3), and QuickJS-only syntax errors lack positions (S1-F4); plus four minor ones (S1-F5..F8).",
      "findingIds": [
        "S1-F1",
        "S1-F2",
        "S1-F3",
        "S1-F4",
        "S1-F5",
        "S1-F6",
